static.solution:
{\mathbf{T} }_u =\frac{\partial \mathrm{\Phi }}{\partial u}=\frac{\partial }{\partial u}\left( u^2- v^2,u+v,u-v\right)= \left\lt  2u,1,1 \right>{\mathbf{T}}_v =\frac{\partial \mathrm{\Phi }}{\partial v}=\frac{\partial }{\partial v}\left( u^2- v^2,u+v,u-v\right)= \left\lt  -2v,1,-1 \right>
The normal is the cross product of {\mathbf{T} }_u and {\mathbf{T} }_v. That is:
\mathbf{n} (u,v)={\mathbf{T} }_u \times {\mathbf{T} }_v = \left|\begin{array}{rrr}
\mathbf{i} \amp \mathbf{j} \amp \mathbf{k} \\2u\amp 1\amp 1\\-2v\amp 1\amp -1
\end{array}\right|=\left|\begin{array}{rr}
1\amp 1\\1\amp -1
\end{array}\right|\mathbf{i}  - \left|\begin{array}{rr}
2u\amp 1\\-2v\amp -1
\end{array}\right|\mathbf{j}  + \left|\begin{array}{cc}
2u\amp 1\\-2v\amp 1
\end{array}\right|\mathbf{k} =-2 \mathbf{i} -2(v-u) \mathbf{j} +2(u+v) \mathbf{k}
= 2 \left\lt -1,u-v,v+u\right>
We compute the normal \mathbf{n}  ( u,v ) at (7,8):
\mathbf{n} (7,8) = 2\left\lt  -1,7-8,8+7 \right> =2 \left\lt -1,-1,15\right> \quad \mathbf{(1)}



We denote the rectangle \mathcal{D}=\left \lbrace(u,v):\,7\le u\le 7.9,\,8\le v\le 8.7\right \rbrace. 


Using the sample point corresponding to u=7, v=8 we obtain the following estimation for the area of S=\mathrm{\Phi}(\mathcal{D}):
\mathrm{Area}(S)\approx \|\mathbf{n} (7,8)\| \mathrm{Area}(\mathcal{D})=\|\mathbf{n} (7,8)\| \cdot 0.9 \cdot 0.7=0.63 \|\mathbf{n} (7,8)\| \quad \mathbf{(2)}
Using \mathbf{(1)} we get 
\|\mathbf{n} (7,8)\|=2\sqrt{(-1)^2+ (-1)^2+ (15)^2}=2\sqrt{227}
Substituting in \mathbf{(2)} gives the following estimation:
\mathrm{Area} (S)\approx 0.63\cdot 2\cdot \sqrt{227}\approx 18.9838\text{.}
